  "correction": "The previous generated-chain receipt correctly recorded refusal for its JSON-round-tripped R14 drawing, but LibreDWG JSON rounded the original MLINESTYLE angle from 1.5707963267948966 to 1.5707963267949 radians. That previous result is not a refusal of the original angle. The generator now reads the original angles from CRC-checked source frames before serializing the corrected graph.",
  "method": [
    "Generate scratch R13/R14/R2000 DWGs using LibreDWG dwgadd. Correct generator-created block graph and DIMSTYLE reference, and restore the exact original style angle observed in the source frame. The three INSERTs use default implicit next links.",
    "Validate original style frame checksum and field boundary, reopen source graph with LibreDWG, and run ASan-instrumented dwg2dxf in strict and explicit partial ASCII/Binary modes.",
    "The deliberately rounded R14 control refuses while preserving destination; the corrected R14 source then succeeds. An ASan adapter test mutates the typed style, verifies refusal and preserved destination, restores it and retries both encodings on the same adapter.",
    "ezdxf independently verifies modelspace INSERT positions and target, following LINE, and block LINE geometry for accepted outputs."
  ],
